The translator's context is not zero-filled on every translation.

QEMU builds with -ftrivial-auto-var-init=zero (meson.build), which makes
the compiler zero every automatic variable where it is declared.
gen_intermediate_code's DisasContext is ~13.6 KB since patch 06 gave it
96 x87/SSE slow blocks, so every TB translation started with a memset of
that size: a preloaded memcpy/memset tracer counted 8.7 GB of it in one
3DMark 99 run on Win98 (673,838 calls, 13,608 bytes each).

The one variable opts out (`__attribute__((uninitialized))`, where the
compiler has it). Nothing reads it before it is set:
i386_tr_init_disas_context initialises the fields the translator uses,
and x87s_new_slow clears each slow block as it hands it out.

Measured on 3DMark 99 (claude98): no change beyond run-to-run noise
(6012 3DMarks, first person 18.4 fps, as before it) -- a benchmark in its
steady state translates little. SSE / x87 / SMC / rep batteries identical,
scripts/test.sh all 57/57. A retranslation-heavy guest (a self-modifying renderer) gains most. No
switch: it changes no behaviour, only what the compiler's hardening flag
adds to one stack frame.

diff --git a/target/i386/tcg/translate.c b/target/i386/tcg/translate.c
index 2115c5cd24..1cd4affc75 100644
--- a/target/i386/tcg/translate.c
+++ b/target/i386/tcg/translate.c
@@ -3613,7 +3613,19 @@ static const TranslatorOps i386_tr_ops = {
 void x86_translate_code(CPUState *cpu, TranslationBlock *tb,
                         int *max_insns, vaddr pc, void *host_pc)
 {
+    /*
+     * Not zero-filled (patch 41): QEMU builds with
+     * -ftrivial-auto-var-init=zero, and patch 06's 96 slow blocks make
+     * this ~13.6 KB, so every translation began with a memset of it --
+     * 8.7 GB in one 3DMark 99 run. i386_tr_init_disas_context sets what
+     * the translator reads and x87s_new_slow clears each slow block it
+     * hands out.
+     */
+#if defined(__has_attribute) && __has_attribute(uninitialized)
+    DisasContext dc __attribute__((uninitialized));
+#else
     DisasContext dc;
+#endif
 
     translator_loop(cpu, tb, max_insns, pc, host_pc, &i386_tr_ops, &dc.base,
                     TCG_TYPE_VA);
